94, the heads turned as both plates show: the warrior's face bowed to Mrs. Helm's shoulder, Black Partridge's in profile to the warrior, each head turned and nodded on its neck with its centre where it was read; on this picture Black Partridge's profile falls on the plate's. Still to model: the faces themselves, the hair (Black Partridge's falling back behind his head is the plate's and not the render's), and the dress of the warrior, Black Partridge, the surgeon and the child] [T-3594, the dress of Black Partridge and the child: Black Partridge's breechcloth is the plates' short apron off his belt, falling over the tops of his thighs and cut at its foot into a ragged fringe (the strands' tips at y 300-312 in this plate, as built through its camera), where the rig's hung to his knee; and the child wears the smock both plates show, from the shoulders to the middle of his thighs, his arms, shins and feet bare, in place of the rig's jacket, trousers and shoes. Still to model: the faces themselves, the hair (Black Partridge's falling back behind his head is the plate's and not the render's), and the dress of the warrior (the fringed sash at his belt) and the surgeon] [T-3594, the hair: Black Partridge's long hair falls out from under the back of his band and streams back and down behind his neck to the back of his left shoulder, a flat lock about 0.06 m across, its end turned up over the shoulder's top, where the plate draws it (x 655-708, y 178-215; through this camera the render's runs from the band's back at y 171 to x 705, y 213); and the warrior's lock hangs from under his band at the side of his bowed head past his cheek, curled at its end (x 512-524, y 220-241), though through this camera it falls on the edge of his head's outline, which the render draws about 12 px left of the plate's, and against his raised arm, so it reads less than the plate's curl. Still to model: the faces themselves, and the dress of the warrior (the fringed sash at his belt) and the surgeon] [T-3594, the warrior's sash: a broad band wrapped round his hips in place of the rig's thin breechcloth, its top across the hips at y 293-298 and its foot sloping down to the west, from y 305 at his front to y 315 at his right hip, the fringed ends flying west out of it (the pouch); the cloth hanging from it at his right hip, in front of his stretched thigh, to its rounded foot at y 352 (x 488-505), and its fall beside the inner side of his raised thigh to y 350 (x 527-540), both where the plate draws them dark. The band stands a few pixels proud of the body's outline east of his hip, where the plate's tucks under Mrs. Helm's hand. Still to model: the faces themselves, and the surgeon's dress] [T-3594, the surgeon's pantaloons: in place of his rig's tight ones, loose heavy cloth on both legs from the hip past the knee to the boot's top, rumpled in creases and gathered over the boot, where the plate draws the leg he stretches west dark and thick from under Mrs. Helm's skirt to the boot (x 465-557, y 385-452, about 20 px through at the shin, as the render's now is). The render's leg runs 10-15 px lower than the plate's at the knee end, inside the pose's reading. Still to model: the faces themselves] [T-3594, the faces turned: Mrs. Helm's face, which looked straight out to the street over a level head, is turned to the warrior and bowed, as this plate draws her head in profile to the west with the brow, nose and chin at its lower left (x 575-590, y 222-242) and the knot of hair at its upper right (x 606-618, y 205-216); the render now draws the same profile, bowed about 30 degrees, the knot behind it. The child's face, which looked straight out, is lifted up and to the right after his hands, as his tilted head here (x 688-715, y 360-385) and Taylor's print show it. Still to model: the sculpted features of the faces themselves (the brows, noses and mouths the plate draws stronger than the rig's neutral face)]; behind the monument (context): the plate shows only the stable's end at its left edge (x 0-97, slate roof, corbel course, quoins) and open ground and the low wall behind the group's left half; the Pullman stable's draft (pullman_house_1729_prairie_ranges) is drawn across x 0-315, about 6 m east of the end the plate shows at its depth. Either the stable's draft or the monument's place (set east and west from the Detroit print's bearing) is out by that much; neither is moved here
